<%# Step 6.3/6.4 — top analytics row. Priority bar, compliance donut and the ticket-level detail %>
<%# table share ONE horizontal band, matching the reference design. It is a 12-column grid rather %>
<%# than three equal thirds so the compact compliance donut only takes the width it needs (3/12) %>
<%# and the detail table gets the freed space (5/12) - priority keeps 4/12. The donut/priority bar %>
<%# both encode the same met/breached/at_risk/no_sla state dimension with the identical color %>
<%# mapping (Global Rule 9); the donut's legend sits BELOW its chart so the card survives its %>
<%# narrow column. tw-items-start keeps the short chart cards top-aligned rather than stretching to %>
<%# the taller detail card's height. The detail card carries its own lg:tw-col-span-5. %>
<div class="tw-grid tw-grid-cols-1 lg:tw-grid-cols-12 tw-gap-6 tw-mb-6 lg:tw-items-start">
  <div class="lg:tw-col-span-4 tw-bg-white tw-border tw-border-gray-200 tw-rounded-xl tw-shadow-sm tw-p-5">
    <%= render 'sla_dashboard/priority_chart' %>
  </div>
  <div class="lg:tw-col-span-3 tw-bg-white tw-border tw-border-gray-200 tw-rounded-xl tw-shadow-sm tw-p-5">
    <%= render 'sla_dashboard/donut_chart' %>
  </div>
  <%# Renders its own lg:tw-col-span-5 card plus the expand-to-modal shell. %>
  <%= render 'sla_dashboard/detail_table' %>
</div>

<%# Full-width row: a dual-line time series wants the page's full horizontal space rather than %>
<%# sharing a one-third column with the row above. %>
<div class="tw-bg-white tw-border tw-border-gray-200 tw-rounded-xl tw-shadow-sm tw-p-5 tw-mb-6">
  <%= render 'sla_dashboard/trend_chart' %>
</div>
